katie oprah's interview has now been  viewed in the uk  what is the reaction there well the  reaction has been one of  astonishment really we had of course  woken up to  headlines based on what you'd seen in  the us but it was only last night that  people actually got to see the  interview in full now interestingly some  saw it as so offensive to the queen that  they actually turned off  after the first hour itv saw a number of  viewers  check out after an hour i mean that may  also be because it was screened quite  late in the uk but  we know that this has created a real  backlash over here  the papers today are full of commentary  articles commentators basically saying  this is harry detonating his family that  really  is the feeling over here how is the  difference  between what u.s viewers thought and  what uk viewers thought  for the most part u.s viewers seem to  back megan and harry meanwhile in the uk  it seems from the polls that we've seen  most people back the monarchy why is  that in america  it was a clear case of team sussex in  terms of who came out  on top i think over here there is a  feeling that  the monarchy has been largely  disrespected by the couple  they feel that the timing of this  interview was very wrong  and that by detonating those bombs  particularly  that suggestion of racism in those  months when i was  pregnant all around this same time  so we have in tandem the conversation of  he won't be  given security he's not going to be  given a title  and also concerns and conversations  about how dark his skin might be when  he's born  what who do people believe made that  statement i mean  just generally what is the consensus of  who that statement could have come from  i think  because of the severity of the  allegations everyone's being very  careful in terms of  naming who it might have been we know  it's not the queen or the duke of  edinburgh because oprah clarified that  i mean senior members of the royal  family are few and far between  it's going to either be prince charles  prince william  or camilla and the inference of course  of it being one of those high-profile  senior members of the royal family  is the question is racism at the heart  of the british monarchy  in the aftermath of this prince charles  was asked about  this interview while he was out and he  did not  bat an eye what do you make of that well  i think the message from  the royal family is today is the  business day as usual we know that their  aids have been locked in crisis meetings  we understand that there may be a  statement possibly later on today  the prince of wales was out on  engagements today sending off a very  clear signal  it's business of usual of course  somebody asked the question about the  interview  and the royals have a deft hand at  avoiding or pretending they can't hear  these questions and  charles moves swiftly on he's clearly  not going to be drawn on this while he  is on an official engagement if  and when the royals do say something i  think it will be a collective statement  out of buckingham palace kensington  palace and clarence house  and i think probably the reason it's  taking some time is because they want to  make sure  they get it right there were reports  that a statement was ready to go on  monday night  before the show aired over here and that  the queen said let's just hold  this statement a lot of people wondering  if that's because she actually wanted to  watch the program  herself when it went out live in america  her aides watched the program and  briefed her the next morning over what  must have been a very awkward  breakfast meeting it is possible that  the queen wanted to sit down and watch  this  for herself but we do understand that it  was the queen  who pressed the pause button on issuing  that statement last night  do you think they know who made that  statement internally  inside the palace do they know who uh  harry was referencing or  do you think they're as baffled as the  rest of the world well i think if this  was a  conversation or conversations between  harry and a member of the royal family i  would imagine that within the family  absolutely it's known who it was that  made those comments  what do you think happens if that  person's name is leaked or that person's  name is or that person is identified  well the problem with all of this  speculation and names being banded  around is that it does cause a huge  amount of damage  suggestions that it might be prince of  wales and that that is why  he and harry have fallen out and harry  has said he feels let down by his father  are very damaging  to the prince of wales's reputation and  you know ditto prince william who's done  a huge amount  to help combat racism in sports  particularly on the football pitch  and who's who's really backing these  anti-racist campaigns over here  in britain so by associating  charles and william with these racist  comments which are alleged to have been  made  to harry it's very damaging for the work  that the royal family is trying to do at  the moment  particularly prince william who's really  been invested  in wiping out racism in british football  he has said  there's no place for racism in this  country what are your sources telling  you about this  meeting this summit of the big three  well it was almost impossible to get  hold of anyone  at any of the households yesterday it  really was a case of lockdown i think  crisis meetings have been going on ever  since the program  aired in the united states i do know  that courteous while they were braced  for  for something explosive they totally  underestimated  just how far harry and megan would go  the talk of the palace is that they  are absolutely horrified by what has  been said they feel that  harry has literally thrown the family  under a bus  the allegations came thick and fast and  i think they  took everyone by surprise what do you  think is going to happen now that kate  and  william have an engagement coming up on  thursday will they  answer questions or will they just do  the as you said  turn a deaf air royal style well the  cambridges have an engagement coming up  on thursday  i think this was always going to be  quite a busy week for the royals the  royals knew there was going to be a  fallout from this interview i don't  think they realized quite how serious  the fallout would be  but this was always due to be a busy  week in the royal calendar and i think  we will see the cambridges absolutely  commit to those engagements in their  diaries they won't want to let anyone  down  but they certainly won't be commenting  on this um in any capacity or an  official engagement  if and when word comes i think it will  come as a joint  statement from all three households  do they need to do something more than  just a joint statement because this is  so damaging and because so many  accusations have been hurled at them  well i think the royal family will be  hoping that people will  judge them the firm the institution  on its work and i think if you look at  the work the queen has done  around the commonwealth which is so  multicultural and so multi-racial  that work speaks for itself prince  william and his work in  trying to stamp out racism in the  british sporting world  again speaks for itself so yes i think  there are calls for a statement but  i do think that the family will be  hoping that people will  will see from what the royals do i think  the royals are hoping that  people will see and understand that  their feeling very much is that there is  no place  for racism in britain one of the  criticisms that the couple is getting  is they requested privacy and yet moved  to the u.s and are taking projects  that keep them in the public eye what do  you think of that i think the issue of  privacy was always going to be something  that was going to come back  and haunt the sussexes i mean don't  forget  that this interview came off the back of  them winning a very high profile  copyright and privacy battle  against the mail on sunday newspaper and  yet here we have a  couple who are fiercely protective of  their private lives they certainly were  over here in the uk sitting down and  giving  not one but two very intimate very  personal interviews and a lot of people  are saying  well how can you ask for privacy  when you're opening up about your  private life it is why the queen  has never given an interview herself she  firmly believes  that once you start talking about your  private life it's impossible to go back  pandora's box has been opened you can't  just put the lid back on  and i think harry and megan may find  themselves in a situation  that if and when they have another  privacy battle on their hands  they may not find that it's in their  favor this time round  because they have been so open about  their private lives  do you think also that maybe the queen  or charles or one of them will break  their silence because of this interview  or will it be business as you they'll  never break their silence  there is clearly a lot of pressure on  the royal family to break their silence  the age-old mantra which has kept the  queen in good stead all of these years  has been  never complain never explained but i  think such is the severity  of these allegations the reverberations  of which are being felt  not just here in britain and across the  pond in the states but around the world  are so serious that there really is a  lot of pressure  for a statement to be released from  buckingham palace with some sort of an  explanation  we do know that crisis talks have been  taking place at the palace ever since  the oprah interview was aired in the  united states i think it has been a case  of lockdown at the palace it's been  almost impossible  to get hold of aids palace spokespeople  and that is because they are working out  the best way to respond i think  if and when it comes it will be a  statement from  all households they will want to show  unity that they are  under huge pressure to give some  explanation  some response to those incredibly  damaging revelations  that there is racism at the heart of the  monarchy i do know  that the queen was at windsor and that  william was back  in london along with charles did they  get on the phone or did they meet in  person  well there have been reports that there  has been a meeting between  charles the queen and prince william and  they are actually in separate parts of  the country but of course the queen is  now very favored soon  and so one imagines that if they've been  speaking it is either over a video  conference call or perhaps on the phone  what does a meeting look like with  charles and the queen and william what's  it like when they get together to talk  are there aids around or is it just the  three of them because our only reference  is really like the crown  i think if you were to use the  sandringham summit earlier this year  where the future of the sussexes was  discussed  that's probably a pretty good template  for what one of these  family crisis meetings looks like of  course that was pre-lockdown they could  meet in person  but they are they are very small it is a  very  um select audience that gets to be a  part of that discussion  and that really is the principles the  queen prince charles and prince william  and their private secretaries and it is  kept as tight as possible for very  obvious reasons  they don't want any leaks

